<%- include('partials/header') %>

<div class="xp-page-header">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="xp-section-label d-block mb-1">Legal</span>
    <h1 class="h3 fw-bold mb-0">Privacy Policy</h1>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container py-4">
  <div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-lg-8">
      <div class="xp-card p-4 mb-4">

        <p class="text-muted small mb-4">Last updated: 1 January 2025</p>

        <h5 class="fw-700 mb-2">1. Who we are</h5>
        <p class="text-muted lh-lg">
          XPSearch is a free platform connecting Year&nbsp;12 and Year&nbsp;13 A-Level students (typically aged 16&ndash;18)
          with employers offering work experience opportunities across the UK. References to &ldquo;we&rdquo;,
          &ldquo;us&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo; mean the XPSearch platform operators.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-700 mb-2 mt-4">2. Our commitment to young people&rsquo;s data</h5>
        <p class="text-muted lh-lg">
          Many of our users are under&nbsp;18. We take this responsibility seriously and comply with the
          <strong>UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK&nbsp;GDPR)</strong> and the
          <strong>Data Protection Act&nbsp;2018</strong>, including the provisions relating to children&rsquo;s data.
          We follow the ICO&rsquo;s <em>Age Appropriate Design Code</em> principles where applicable.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-700 mb-2 mt-4">3. What data we collect</h5>
        <p class="text-muted lh-lg">We only collect the minimum information needed to run the platform:</p>
        <div class="table-responsive">
          <table class="table table-sm text-muted small">
            <thead class="table-light">
              <tr><th>Data</th><th>Who provides it</th><th>Why we need it</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Full name</td><td>All users</td><td>To identify you on the platform</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Email address</td><td>All users</td><td>Account login; employers contact accepted applicants</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Password (hashed)</td><td>All users</td><td>Secure account access &mdash; stored using bcrypt, never in plain text</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Year group (12 or 13)</td><td>Students</td><td>To match you with appropriate opportunities</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Company name</td><td>Employers</td><td>To display alongside job listings</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Cover letters</td><td>Students</td><td>Submitted voluntarily when applying for a role</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted lh-lg">
          We do <strong>not</strong> collect date of birth, home address, phone number, school name,
          photographs, or any special-category data.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-700 mb-2 mt-4">4. Lawful basis for processing</h5>
        <p class="text-muted lh-lg">
          We process personal data on the basis of <strong>consent</strong> (Article&nbsp;6(1)(a) UK&nbsp;GDPR).
          When you register, you explicitly consent to us processing your data for the purposes described in this policy.
          You may withdraw consent at any time by deleting your account (see Section&nbsp;8).
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-700 mb-2 mt-4">5. How we protect student data</h5>
        <ul class="text-muted lh-lg">
          <li class="mb-2">
            <strong>Email addresses are hidden</strong> &mdash; an employer can only see a student&rsquo;s email
            address after they have <em>accepted</em> the student&rsquo;s application. This prevents unnecessary
            disclosure of minors&rsquo; contact information.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-2">
            <strong>Passwords are hashed</strong> using bcrypt and are never stored or transmitted in plain text.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-2">
            <strong>CSRF protection</strong> prevents cross-site request forgery attacks on all forms.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-2">
            <strong>Rate limiting</strong> protects against brute-force login attempts.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-2">
            <strong>Session cookies</strong> are httpOnly and use the SameSite attribute to prevent cross-site misuse.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-2">
            <strong>No tracking</strong> &mdash; we do not use analytics, advertising cookies, or third-party trackers.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h5 class="fw-700 mb-2 mt-4">6. Who can see your data</h5>
        <div class="table-responsive">
          <table class="table table-sm text-muted small">
            <thead class="table-light">
              <tr><th>Your data</th><th>Who can see it</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Name &amp; year group</td><td>Employers you apply to</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Email address (students)</td><td>Only employers who <strong>accept</strong> your application</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Cover letter</td><td>The employer for the role you applied to</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Company name (employers)</td><td>All visitors (shown on job listings)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Password</td><td>Nobody &mdash; stored as an irreversible hash</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted lh-lg">
          We do <strong>not</strong> sell, share, or transfer personal data to any third parties.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-700 mb-2 mt-4">7. Data retention</h5>
        <p class="text-muted lh-lg">
          We keep your data for as long as your account exists. If you delete your account (see below),
          all of your personal data is permanently removed from our database immediately.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-700 mb-2 mt-4">8. Your rights</h5>
        <p class="text-muted lh-lg">Under UK&nbsp;GDPR you have the right to:</p>
        <ul class="text-muted lh-lg">
          <li class="mb-2"><strong>Access</strong> your personal data &mdash; visible on your <a href="/profile">Profile</a> page.</li>
          <li class="mb-2"><strong>Rectify</strong> inaccurate data &mdash; you can update your name, company, and password on your Profile page.</li>
          <li class="mb-2"><strong>Erase</strong> your data (&ldquo;right to be forgotten&rdquo;) &mdash; use the <strong>Delete Account</strong> option on your Profile page. This permanently deletes your account, applications, job listings, and all associated data.</li>
          <li class="mb-2"><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> &mdash; you can stop us processing your data at any time by deleting your account.</li>
        </ul>

        <h5 class="fw-700 mb-2 mt-4">9. Parental / guardian information</h5>
        <p class="text-muted lh-lg">
          Under UK law the age of consent for data processing is <strong>13</strong>. Our users are aged 16&ndash;18,
          so parental consent is not legally required. However, we encourage students to inform a parent or guardian
          that they are using XPSearch. During registration, students confirm that they are aged 16 or over and that
          a parent or guardian is aware they are using the platform.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-700 mb-2 mt-4">10. Cookies</h5>
        <p class="text-muted lh-lg">
          We use only <strong>strictly necessary cookies</strong> for session management and CSRF protection.
          We do not use advertising, analytics, or preference cookies. Because these cookies are essential
          for the site to function, separate cookie consent is not required under UK&nbsp;GDPR.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-700 mb-2 mt-4">11. Changes to this policy</h5>
        <p class="text-muted lh-lg">
          If we make material changes to this policy, we will update the &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date at the top
          of this page. We encourage you to review this policy periodically.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
